    "p": {
      "type": "npc",
      "name": "Professor Brassbolt",
      "style": "professor",
      "lines": [
        "Ah! A new apprentice! Welcome to Cogsworth, the city that runs on steam... and on Python.",
        "Every chest and caged relic in this city is sealed by a puzzle-lock. The locks only open for working code.",
        "Walk up to a chest and press E. You'll get a problem, a code editor, and a set of tests. Make every test pass and the lock springs open!",
        "Each lock you open gives you a Brass Cog. Collect six and the great gate to the Aetherforge Foundry, east of here, will open for you.",
        "Stuck? Every lock has hints. Using them is no shame; every engineer started as an apprentice. Now off you go!"
      ]
    },
    "q": {
      "type": "npc",
      "name": "Foreman Ironside",
      "style": "foreman",
      "lines": [
        "So the Professor's apprentice made it through the gate. Good. The Foundry is no place for loops and lists alone.",
        "Here we build with classes, stacks, linked lists, recursion and sorting algorithms. Proper engineering.",
        "The Grand Engine sits in the vault to the south-east. Its door won't budge for fewer than twelve cogs.",
        "Power up the Engine and you'll have done what no engineer has done in a hundred years. Get to it!"
      ]
    },
